WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
Who do you say that I am?

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.160
In Mark, Peter answers:
You are the Christ.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.870
In Luke: The Christ of God.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.650
In Matthew, he adds: the
Son of the living God.

5
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.500
Before any Gospel was written, stories
like this were told aloud for decades,

6
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.300
in preaching, worship and debate.

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.650
So can we trace what happened
to them on the way to the page?

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.940
In this mission, you'll meet the tools
scholars use to study each stage,

9
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.710
from spoken word to finished Gospel.

10
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.830
Then you will weigh up how much these methods
really help us understand the Gospels.

11
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.690
Your mission: find out how scholars trace
the stories of Jesus from telling to

12
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.400
writing.
